# Cloudflare (and Netlify) redirect rules — the port of netlify.toml's
# [[redirects]] blocks, kept in the same order because both hosts take the
# first match. Netlify's own toml rules still win while it deploys the
# rollback, so the two must stay identical until cleanup deletes netlify.toml.
#
# Exact paths, not wildcards, wherever a category sits under the same prefix:
# `/features/*` here would swallow every feature and category page.
#
# Cloudflare has no trailing-slash normalization, so each path is listed both
# ways — the same shape netlify.toml already used.

# Retired /features/ hub → the homepage tour, which lists the five categories.
/features                /#features               301
/features/               /#features               301

# Legacy Webflow paths → Astro marketing site
/features/sharing        /features/share/         301
/features/sharing/       /features/share/         301
/features/recall         /features/suggestions/   301
/features/recall/        /features/suggestions/   301

/updates                 /release-notes/          301
/updates/*               /release-notes/          301
/changelog               /release-notes/          301
/changelog/              /release-notes/          301
/changelog/*             /release-notes/:splat    301

/release-notes/page/1    /release-notes/          301
/release-notes/page/1/   /release-notes/          301
